    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Four-week review after starting amlodipine, two weeks after influenza. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Sir John has taken amlodipine 5 mg every morning for four weeks. Two weeks ago he had influenza A, treated with five days of oseltamivir; the fever settled in three days, and he is left with a dry cough on cold mornings and tires earlier than usual on his walks, though he is walking two to three miles again. His home readings for the past week average 134/84. He has no ankle swelling, dizziness or flushing. He has lost 1.8 kg since intake. He had his echocardiogram this morning and brought a urine sample. His exercise treadmill test, booked for today, was postponed at the sick visit until he has been back to his usual activity for two weeks. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Home readings</td><td>Seven-day average 134/84 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza</td><td>Recovering; dry morning cough; tires earlier</td></tr><tr><td>Amlodipine</td><td>No side effects</td></tr><tr><td>Echocardiogram</td><td>Ejection fraction 62%; mild concentric remodeling</td></tr><tr><td>Urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio</td><td>12 mg/g</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

