    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Essential hypertension on amlodipine (I10)</content>. Home average down from 144/90 to 134/84, not yet below 130/80. Weight is falling and he has just been ill, so the dose is kept and blood pressure is rechecked at the preventive visit in two weeks; if it is still above goal at eight weeks, amlodipine will go to 10 mg. Echocardiogram shows a normal ejection fraction and mild concentric remodeling without hypertrophy; urine albumin normal. [S]<list><item>Continue amlodipine 5 mg.</item><item>Home readings weekly.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Influenza A (J10.1)</content>. Recovered, with a post-viral cough that is fading; lungs clear. [S]<list><item>No antibiotic; return if the cough worsens or he becomes breathless.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Expedition preparation (Z71.84)</content>. The exercise treadmill test should wait until two weeks of usual activity after the influenza. [S]<list><item>Exercise test at the eight-week review.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Office blood pressure (seated, five minutes&apos; rest, large cuff, average of two readings)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>136/84 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Home blood pressure monitoring</td><td>At diagnosis and two to four weeks after each treatment change, then weekly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Average 134/84 mmHg four weeks after starting amlodipine</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight, BMI and waist</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>89.0 kg, BMI 30.8</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Cardiac auscultation</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No murmur or gallop</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio</td><td>At diagnosis, then yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>12 mg/g, normal; the sample deferred from intake</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Basic metabolic panel, potassium and eGFR</td><td>Yearly (every six months only on a diuretic or renin-angiotensin blocker)</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Not needed for amlodipine; yearly</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Echocardiogram</td><td>At diagnosis of stage 2 hypertension or suspected left ventricular hypertrophy</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Ejection fraction 62%; mild concentric remodeling, septum 11 mm; normal valves</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Amlodipine safety: ankle swelling, dizziness, flushing</td><td>At each visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No ankle swelling, dizziness or flushing</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Exercise treadmill test before strenuous remote work</td><td>Before clearance</td><td>Due</td><td>Postponed at the sick visit until two weeks of usual activity after influenza; rebooked for the eight-week review</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Wilderness and expedition medicine consultation</td><td>Before clearance for remote duty</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Seen four weeks ago</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Confirm or exclude hypertension with a week of home readings. Outcome by 1845-01-27: Home average 144/90 mmHg: stage 2 hypertension confirmed [S]</item><item>Blood pressure below 130/80 mmHg at home before departure. In progress; target 1845-04-07 [S]</item><item>Lose about 5 percent of body weight before sailing by his own plan of walking, hill work and smaller portions. In progress; target 1845-05-05 [S]</item><item>Medical clearance for the command with a written expedition health plan, medical kit and evacuation plan. In progress; target 1845-05-05 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, hypertension and hyperlipidemia monographs (2026); Weight Loss to Prevent Obesity-Related Morbidity and Mortality in Adults: Behavioral Interventions (2018); Clinical Practice Guidelines by the Infectious Diseases Society of America: 2018 Update on Diagnosis, Treatment, Chemoprophylaxis, and Institutional Outbreak Management of Seasonal Influenza (2018)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Preventive visit with vaccinations in two weeks. Eight-week review with the exercise treadmill test. Call for breathlessness or a worsening cough. Next scheduled visit 1845-03-10: periodic adult preventive visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

